{
 "ep": 15,
 "total": 140,
 "title": "Start, Stop, Restart and Reload PostgreSQL",
 "phase": "Installation & Administration",
 "lines": [
  {
   "say": "Restart or reload? A DBA must know the difference.",
   "cap": "*Restart* or *reload?* Know the *difference.*"
  },
  {
   "say": "This is episode fifteen of the PostgreSQL DBA series: four server actions, and when to use each.",
   "cap": "Episode 15: *start,* *stop,* *restart,* *reload.*",
   "cue": "four"
  },
  {
   "say": "The tool is pg_ctl. Dash capital D tells it which data directory to control.",
   "cap": "*pg_ctl* controls one server. *-D* picks the data directory.",
   "cue": "tool"
  },
  {
   "say": "Start runs the server in the background. Use dash l, or a redirect, to log its output.",
   "cap": "*start* runs it in the background. *-l* writes a *log.*",
   "cue": "Start"
  },
  {
   "say": "Stop shuts the server down. Restart is simply a stop, followed by a start.",
   "cap": "*stop* shuts down. *restart* = stop + start.",
   "cue": "Restart"
  },
  {
   "say": "Reload only sends a SIGHUP signal. The server rereads its config files, and sessions stay connected.",
   "cap": "*reload* sends *SIGHUP.* Config files are *reread.*",
   "cue": "rereads"
  },
  {
   "say": "Here it is on a test cluster. Start waits until the server is ready, then prints: server started.",
   "cap": "start *waits,* then prints *server started.*",
   "cue": "waits"
  },
  {
   "say": "Reload prints one line: server signaled. Restart shows a full stop, then a full start.",
   "cap": "reload: *server signaled.* restart: *stop,* then *start.*",
   "cue": "Restart"
  },
  {
   "say": "Stop has three modes, chosen with dash m. Smart waits for every client to disconnect.",
   "cap": "Three modes with *-m.* *smart* waits for clients.",
   "cue": "Smart"
  },
  {
   "say": "Fast is the default. It rolls back active transactions, disconnects clients, then shuts down.",
   "cap": "*fast* is the *default:* rolls back, disconnects.",
   "cue": "default"
  },
  {
   "say": "Immediate aborts all server processes without a clean shutdown, so the next start runs crash recovery.",
   "cap": "*immediate:* no clean shutdown, *crash* *recovery* next.",
   "cue": "aborts"
  },
  {
   "say": "After an immediate stop, our test log says: automatic recovery in progress. Output trimmed.",
   "cap": "Log: *automatic* *recovery* in progress.",
   "cue": "automatic"
  },
  {
   "say": "The docs: use immediate only in emergencies, and avoid SIGKILL on the server.",
   "cap": "*Immediate* only in *emergencies.* Avoid *kill -9.*",
   "cue": "SIGKILL"
  },
  {
   "say": "So when is reload enough? Every setting has a context, shown in pg_settings.",
   "cap": "Every setting has a *context* in *pg_settings.*",
   "cue": "context"
  },
  {
   "say": "postmaster means restart only, like shared_buffers. work_mem is a user setting, so reload is enough.",
   "cap": "*postmaster* = restart only. *work_mem:* reload is enough.",
   "cue": "work_mem"
  },
  {
   "say": "ALTER SYSTEM sets log_min_duration_statement to five hundred milliseconds. Then, pg_reload_conf.",
   "cap": "*ALTER SYSTEM,* then *pg_reload_conf().*",
   "cue": "pg_reload_conf"
  },
  {
   "say": "SHOW returns five hundred milliseconds. It applied, with no restart.",
   "cap": "*500ms.* Applied with *no restart.*",
   "cue": "applied"
  },
  {
   "say": "Now we set shared_buffers to two hundred fifty six megabytes, and reload again.",
   "cap": "Now *shared_buffers* to *256MB,* and reload.",
   "cue": "reload"
  },
  {
   "say": "SHOW still says one hundred twenty eight megabytes, and pending_restart is true.",
   "cap": "Still *128MB.* *pending_restart* is *true.*",
   "cue": "pending_restart"
  },
  {
   "say": "After a restart, SHOW returns two hundred fifty six megabytes.",
   "cap": "After *restart:* *256MB.*",
   "cue": "returns"
  },
  {
   "say": "Common mistake: trusting reload. With a typo in postgresql.conf, pg_reload_conf still returned true.",
   "cap": "A *typo,* and reload *still* returned *true.*",
   "cue": "true"
  },
  {
   "say": "Invalid settings are ignored, but logged. pg_file_settings shows the bad entry.",
   "cap": "*pg_file_settings* shows the *error.*",
   "cue": "shows"
  },
  {
   "say": "DBA takeaway, a common practice: reload, check pending_restart and the log, and plan restarts for a maintenance window.",
   "cap": "Reload, *check,* and plan *restarts* in a *window.*",
   "cue": "plan"
  },
  {
   "say": "Recap: reload rereads the config files, and restart is a stop plus a start.",
   "cap": "Recap: *reload* rereads, *restart* = stop + start.",
   "cue": "restart"
  },
  {
   "say": "Fast is the default stop, immediate means crash recovery, and context tells you what needs a restart.",
   "cap": "*fast* default, *immediate* recovers, check *context.*",
   "cue": "context"
  },
  {
   "say": "Next up: creating and dropping databases safely. Follow so you don't miss it, and send this to a friend who's learning PostgreSQL.",
   "cap": "Next up: *create* and *drop* databases. *Follow* and share."
  }
 ],
